          "content": "{\n  \"_doc\": \"Copy to the project as verification.json and fill it. Paths are relative to `root` (relative to this file). Delete a key to switch that check off. Keys starting with _ are ignored. Regexes are Python, escaped for JSON (\\\\d, \\\\|).\",\n\n  \"root\": \"docs/my-deliverable\",\n\n  \"_registries\": \"Files that hold ids, one per row. Rows are counted, not unique ids. md: `row_regex` with ONE group = the full id. csv: id column. Used by counts, references, required_mentions and next_id.py.\",\n  \"registries\": {\n    \"findings\": {\"file\": \"findings.md\", \"row_regex\": \"^\\\\| (F-\\\\d{3}) \"},\n    \"backlog\": {\"file\": \"backlog.csv\", \"csv\": {\"delimiter\": \";\", \"id_column\": \"id\"}}\n  },\n\n  \"_counts\": \"Numbers written in prose must equal the registry row count. `regex` has TWO groups: number and label; `labels` maps each label (case-insensitive) to a registry.\",\n  \"counts\": [\n    {\"files\": [\"parts/00-summary.md\"], \"regex\": \"\\\\*{0,2}(\\\\d+)\\\\*{0,2} (findings|backlog items)\",\n     \"labels\": {\"findings\": \"findings\", \"backlog items\": \"backlog\"}}\n  ],\n\n  \"_references\": \"Every id cited in `files` must exist in `registry`. The generated document is excluded automatically.\",\n  \"references\": [\n    {\"files\": [\"**/*.md\"], \"exclude\": [\"findings.md\"], \"regex\": \"\\\\bF-\\\\d{3}\\\\b\", \"registry\": \"findings\"}\n  ],\n\n  \"_index\": \"Every file the index cites (regex group 1) must exist in one of `search` folders, and every file matching `must_list` globs must be cited (a new part nobody added to the index fails).\",\n  \"index\": {\"file\": \"00-INDEX.md\", \"regex\": \"`([\\\\w\\\\-./]+\\\\.(?:md|csv))`\", \"search\": [\".\"], \"must_list\": [\"parts/*.md\"]},\n\n  \"_document\": \"Single generated deliverable (build.py). `sections` in order: a part path, or {csv, title, delimiter} for a table. `{date}` in notice is today's date; only the date in the title/notice lines is ignored when checking it is up to date. Optional: `separator` between sections (default \\\"\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n\\\").\",\n  \"document\": {\n    \"output\": \"DELIVERABLE.md\",\n    \"title\": \"# My deliverable\",\n    \"notice\": \"> Generated on {date} by `build.py`. Do not edit here: edit the parts and rebuild.\",\n    \"sections\": [\"parts/00-summary.md\", \"parts/01-area.md\", \"findings.md\",\n                 {\"csv\": \"backlog.csv\", \"title\": \"## Backlog\", \"delimiter\": \";\"}]\n  },\n\n  \"_source_coverage\": \"Every source file must be cited (file name, or stem with match=stem) in at least one of `cited_in`.\",\n  \"source_coverage\": [{\"sources\": \"sources/**/*.png\", \"cited_in\": [\"parts/*.md\"], \"match\": \"name\"}],\n\n  \"_forbidden\": \"Personal data and secrets. defaults=true adds CPF, phone, e-mail, secret. `allow` regexes whitelist a match (e.g. the company domain).\",\n  \"forbidden\": {\"files\": [\"**/*.md\"], \"exclude\": [\"sources/**\"], \"defaults\": true,\n                \"patterns\": {\"internal host\": \"\\\\binternal\\\\.example\\\\b\"}, \"allow\": [\"@mycompany\\\\.com\"]},\n\n  \"_required_mentions\": \"Terms that must appear in `files`: an explicit list, and/or every id of `registry` from `since` on (e.g. findings added after the last review must reach the summary).\",\n  \"required_mentions\": [{\"terms\": [\"Out of scope\"], \"registry\": \"findings\", \"since\": \"F-010\", \"files\": [\"parts/00-summary.md\"]}],\n\n  \"_loop_counter\": \"execution-loop folder: 'NN Name.md' files numbered from 00 with no gap or repeat.\",\n  \"loop_counter\": {\"folder\": \"../../.agents/plans/execution-loops/2026_01_01/My Goal\"},\n\n  \"_unique_columns\": \"CSV columns whose values must not repeat.\",\n  \"unique_columns\": [{\"file\": \"catalog.csv\", \"delimiter\": \";\", \"column\": \"name\"}],\n\n  \"_custom_checks\": \"Python file (relative to this config) with functions check_<name>(ctx) -> (ok, evidence); ctx has root (Path), config and registries ({name: [ids]}). A crash counts as FAIL.\",\n  \"custom_checks\": \"verification_custom.py\"\n}\n"
