          "content": "# Copy Structure Reference\n\nDetailed requirements for each landing page section.\n\n## 1. Hero Section\n\n### Requirements\n- **Title**: ≤70 characters, must communicate category + differentiator\n- **Subtitle**: ≤150 characters, expands on the value proposition\n- **CTA**: ≤20 characters, action-oriented\n- **Image**: Specify what visual represents the product\n\n### Title Formula\nAnswer two questions:\n1. What is this? (category)\n2. Why is it different? (key differentiator)\n\n**Examples:**\n- \"O primeiro CRM que preenche dados sozinho\" (CRM + auto-fill differentiator)\n- \"Meeting notes that write themselves\" (Meeting tool + AI differentiator)\n\n### Subtitle Formula\nExpand on the HOW and WHO:\n- How the differentiator works\n- Who benefits most\n\n### Hero Image Spec\nInclude:\n- What to show (product screenshot, mockup, illustration)\n- Key elements that should be visible\n- Mood/style aligned with design system\n\n---\n\n## 2. Social Proof Section\n\n### Options (pick one or combine)\n1. **User count**: \"Usado por mais de X.XXX usuários\"\n2. **Company logos**: \"Empresas como [Logo1], [Logo2], [Logo3] já usam\"\n3. **Rating**: \"Avaliação 4.9 ★★★★★\"\n4. **Certification**: Relevant trust badges\n\n### Guidelines\n- Use real numbers if available\n- If no data, suggest realistic placeholder with note to update\n- Logos should be recognizable to target audience\n\n---\n\n## 3. Product vs. Alternatives Section\n\n### Structure\nCompare the product against top 2-3 alternatives identified in positioning.\n\n### Format Options\n\n**Option A: Table comparison**\n| Feature | [Product] | [Alternative 1] | [Alternative 2] |\n|---------|-----------|-----------------|-----------------|\n| [Unique feature 1] | ✓ | ✗ | ✗ |\n| [Unique feature 2] | ✓ | Partial | ✗ |\n\n**Option B: Before/After narrative**\n- \"Antes: [pain with alternatives]\"\n- \"Depois: [benefit with product]\"\n\n**Option C: Side-by-side cards**\n- Card 1: \"Com [Alternative]\" - list pain points\n- Card 2: \"Com [Product]\" - list benefits\n\n### Guidelines\n- Focus ONLY on differentiators\n- Be factual, not aggressive\n- Show clear winner without being negative\n\n---\n\n## 4. Features & Value Section\n\n### Structure\nFor each unique feature (3-5 features max):\n- **Title**: Feature name (≤40 chars)\n- **Description**: Benefit explanation (≤100 chars)\n- **Visual**: Screenshot or illustration spec\n\n### Guidelines\n- ONLY include features that competitors don't have\n- Table stakes features are implied by the category\n- Each feature must map to a value theme from positioning\n- Order by importance to target customer\n\n### Visual Spec Format\n```\n[Generate] or [Screenshot needed]\n- Screen: [which product screen to show]\n- Highlight: [which element to emphasize]\n- Context: [what user action is being shown]\n```\n\n---\n\n## 5. How It Works Section\n\n### Structure\n3-5 steps maximum, showing the user journey:\n\n**Step format:**\n- **Number**: 1, 2, 3...\n- **Title**: Action verb + object (≤30 chars)\n- **Description**: What happens (≤80 chars)\n- **Visual**: Icon or mini-screenshot\n\n### Guidelines\n- Start from user's first action\n- End with achieved outcome\n- Keep steps simple and sequential\n- Avoid technical jargon\n\n---\n\n## 6. Testimonials Section\n\n### Structure\n3-4 testimonials that reinforce competitive claims.\n\n**Testimonial format:**\n```\n\"[Quote that mentions specific differentiator or comparison to alternative]\"\n— [Name], [Role that matches ICP], [Company type if relevant]\n```\n\n### Guidelines for Invented Testimonials\n- Role must match the target customer profile from positioning\n- Quote must reinforce a specific competitive claim\n- Reference the alternative they stopped using\n- Sound natural, not marketing-speak\n\n**Example:**\n```\n\"Depois que conheci o [Product], nunca mais voltei para planilhas. \nO que levava 2 horas agora leva 5 minutos.\"\n— Marina Costa, Head de Operações, Startup de Logística\n```\n\n### Note to User\nMark invented testimonials clearly:\n```\n[SUGESTÃO - substituir por depoimento real se disponível]\n```\n\n---\n\n## 7. Target Customers Section\n\n### Structure\n3-4 cards showing ideal customer profiles.\n\n**Card format:**\n- **Persona title**: Role or type (e.g., \"Product Managers\", \"Solo Founders\")\n- **Description**: Why this product is perfect for them (≤80 chars)\n- **Icon or illustration**: Visual representation\n\n### Guidelines\n- Based on target customer characteristics from positioning\n- Show the BEHAVIOR or SITUATION that makes them ideal\n- Not demographics, but psychographics\n\n---\n\n## 8. CTA Section\n\n### Structure\n- **Headline**: Emotional/aspirational (≤60 chars)\n- **Supporting points**: 2-3 bullet points addressing objections\n- **CTA button**: Same as hero CTA\n- **Trust element**: Risk reducer (free trial, money-back, etc.)\n\n### Guidelines\n- Headline should paint the desired outcome\n- Bullet points remove friction (time, risk, complexity)\n- CTA should be identical to hero for consistency\n\n---\n\n## 9. FAQ Section\n\n### Structure\n5-7 questions that address common objections.\n\n**Categories to cover:**\n1. **Price/Value**: \"How much does it cost?\" / \"Is there a free trial?\"\n2. **Trust/Security**: \"Is my data safe?\" / \"Who else uses this?\"\n3. **Effort/Time**: \"How long to set up?\" / \"Do I need technical skills?\"\n4. **Comparison**: \"How is this different from [Alternative]?\"\n5. **Support**: \"What if I need help?\"\n\n### Guidelines\n- Questions should be in customer's voice\n- Answers should be concise and confident\n- Use objections identified in positioning analysis\n- End answers with subtle CTAs when appropriate\n\n---\n\n## 10. Footer Section\n\n### Standard Elements\n- Logo\n- Navigation links (Features, Pricing, About, Contact)\n- Legal links (Privacy Policy, Terms of Service)\n- Social media links (if applicable)\n- Trust badges/certifications\n- Copyright notice\n\n### Guidelines\n- Keep minimal and clean\n- Include only essential links\n- Match design system colors\n"
